## One city report, written as a plain sequential program.
## The machine overlaps everything the sequential run cannot tell apart:
## - the two `parallel` arms and the independent `traffic` lookup;
## - the district surveys, which do not wait for the storm branch to resolve;
## - one survey per district, all at once.
@def (city: str, districts: list)report(summary, scores):
    ()parallel(`a`, `b`)
    a:
        (city)weather(sky)
    b:
        (city)events(n_events)
    (city)traffic(jam)
    (sky)is_stormy(storm)
    (storm)branch(`warn`, `calm`)
    warn:
        (city)alert(note)
    calm:
        note = "clear"
    scores = []
    (districts)each(district, `one`)
    one:
        (city, district)survey(score)
        (scores, score)append(scores)
    (sky, n_events, jam, note, scores)compose(summary)
